module fluorescence

// NOTE: the source protocol (Table 3 / Fig. 3) is a bench-scale flask/plate procedure, not a
// droplet-based one. BioScript has no primitives for the paper's <move> (spatial relocation of
// a vessel between locations) or <rename> (renaming a vessel after a state change) experiment
// actions, so only the material-transformation core -- adding YPD medium, inoculating with a
// yeast colony, and incubating -- is represented below. Shaking speed (200 rpm) is likewise not
// expressible, since BioScript's 'heat' primitive only carries temperature and duration.

manifest ypd_medium
manifest yeast_colony

instructions:

// add 15: 50 ml YPD medium into the (to become) yeast culture flask
ypd = dispense 500 units of ypd_medium

// add 17: single yeast colony (small volume) inoculated into the YPD medium
colony = dispense 1 units of yeast_colony
yeast_culture = mix ypd with colony

// incubate 20: shaking incubation at 30 C for 12-24 h until the medium becomes cloudy
// (upper bound of the stated 12-24 h range used below)
heat yeast_culture at 30c for 1440m

dispose yeast_culture
